{"_meta":{"as_of":"2026-08-12T08:05:16+00:00","coverage":"12/12","note":"Earnings dates and consensus from Yahoo Finance \u2014 often estimated rather than company-confirmed, so treat them as approximate until close. Policy and catalyst entries are hand-dated in the research files."},"events":[{"d":"2026-07-28","type":"policy","t":"LIVE \u2014 FCC Covered List now bars foreign-produced robots (Jul 28, 2026)","why":"Adopted, not proposed. Any ground-moving device over 4.4lb (with dock) that senses, connects and navigates cannot get FCC equipment authorisation unless the Department of War grants a Conditional Approval. Read the carve-outs before pricing it: industrial robotic ARMS, medical robots, vehicles and drones are explicitly excluded, so Fanuc, Yaskawa, ABB, KUKA/Midea, Estun and Doosan's cobots are untouched. What is caught is humanoids, quadrupeds and autonomous mobile robots \u2014 9880.HK UBTech head-on, 277810.KQ Rainbow Robotics and TER's MiR unit on the same terms despite being allied, plus 1810.HK Xiaomi's consumer line. HSAI is hit second-hand through its customers' US market access. The asymmetry is the point: US-produced humanoids get a market cleared by rule, everyone else queues for a discretionary exemption.","hits":"act, sen"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"policy","t":"Chinese WFE tools qualifying at Samsung and SK Hynix","why":"Reuters, Aug 4 2026: both Korean memory makers have been testing AMEC etch tools for their China fabs \u2014 begun ~2 years ago, aimed at SERVICING and upgrading existing lines rather than adding capacity, after Washington revoked their validated-end-user status in 2025 and replaced it with an annual licence. Small in units, large in meaning: qualification is the slow half of the WFE moat, and it is being done by the two customers whose sign-off other buyers copy. Deutsche Bank has NAURA, AMEC, Piotech and ACM Research each clearing $1B of revenue in 2026 and together taking 25-30% of China's ~$28B WFE market. This is the external bear case (see Thesis) arriving as an event rather than an opinion \u2014 watch whether qualification stays confined to China fabs.","hits":"wfe"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"earnings","tk":"7011.T","n":"Mitsubishi Heavy Industries","conv":2,"froth":2,"dd":-22.7,"ts":1785825000,"when":"post","xt":"15:30 JST","rep":{"act":40.08,"est":23.93,"when":"2026-08-04","surp":67.5,"move":-0.99,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-05","type":"earnings","tk":"6481.T","n":"THK","conv":2,"froth":1,"dd":-13.3,"ts":1785911400,"when":"post","xt":"15:30 JST","rep":{"act":261.09,"est":89.25,"when":"2026-08-04","surp":192.6,"move":-2.46,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-05","type":"earnings","tk":"ENR.DE","n":"Siemens Energy","conv":2,"froth":2,"eps":1.32,"eps_lo":1.21,"eps_hi":1.42,"dd":-17.6,"ts":1785943800,"when":"post","xt":"17:30 CEST","rep":{"act":1.31,"est":1.19,"when":"2026-08-04","surp":10.6,"move":2.56,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-05","type":"earnings","tk":"IFX.DE","n":"Infineon","conv":2,"froth":1,"eps":0.62,"eps_lo":0.59,"eps_hi":0.64,"dd":-28.9,"ts":1785943800,"when":"post","xt":"17:30 CEST","rep":{"act":0.44,"est":0.44,"when":"2026-08-04","surp":-0.6,"move":0.51,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-06","type":"earnings","tk":"5801.T","n":"Furukawa Electric","conv":2,"froth":1,"dd":-34.3,"ts":1785997800,"when":"post","xt":"15:30 JST","rep":{"act":31.6,"est":24.27,"when":"2026-08-05","surp":30.2,"move":2.49,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-06","type":"earnings","tk":"SIE.DE","n":"Siemens","conv":2,"froth":1,"eps":2.75,"eps_lo":2.61,"eps_hi":2.86,"dd":-3.7,"ts":1786030200,"when":"post","xt":"17:30 CEST","rep":{"act":3.14,"est":2.75,"when":"2026-08-06","surp":14.2,"move":1.19,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-07","type":"earnings","tk":"6324.T","n":"Harmonic Drive Systems","conv":3,"froth":2,"dd":-28.2,"ts":1786084200,"when":"post","xt":"15:30 JST","rep":{"act":13.46,"est":10.6,"when":"2026-08-06","surp":27.0,"move":-10.89,"live":true}},{"d":"2026-08-10","type":"earnings","tk":"CAMT","n":"Camtek","conv":2,"